ActRaiser Recomp  (@SNESBUILD_OS_NAME@/@SNESBUILD_ARCH_NAME@)
Version @SNESBUILD_VERSION@

This builds and runs the game on your computer from a game ROM you already
own. Everything needed is already in this folder. You do NOT need to install
anything.


WHAT YOU NEED
-------------
Your own game ROM: a ".sfc" or ".smc" file. Nothing else.


HOW TO PLAY
-----------
1. Start "@SNESBUILD_RUN_SCRIPT@":
      macOS    - double-click  run-build.command
      Windows  - double-click  run-build.bat
      Linux    - run           ./run-build.sh

2. Your browser opens the private local builder. Choose your ROM, then press
   "Build game". This takes a few minutes and only needs to be done one time.
   Your ROM never leaves this computer.

3. Play - when the build finishes, a "run-game" file appears in this folder
   (run-game.command on macOS, run-game.bat on Windows, run-game.sh on Linux).
   Press "Play" in the builder now. Later you can either open the run-game file
   directly, or start run-build again: it notices the game is already built and
   opens as a launcher, so there is nothing to rebuild and no ROM to choose.


UPGRADING TO A NEWER VERSION
----------------------------
Extract the new package over the top of this folder. Your settings, saves, and
anything you customised are kept - the new version's settings are merged in
alongside them, and you will see a line like

      [upgrade] config.ini: 2 new settings added, your values kept

the next time you play. If you changed a setting, your value always wins; only
settings that are genuinely new in that version get added.

The same is true of "diorama-layers.ini" and "game-assets/manifest.ini": your
authored rooms and your own asset entries survive an upgrade.

You will need your ROM again only if you want to REBUILD. If you just want to
keep playing, the game is already built and nothing else is needed.


OPTIONAL: FREE UP SPACE WHEN YOU ARE DONE BUILDING
--------------------------------------------------
Most of this folder is the build toolchain, and it is only needed if you want to
build again later. After a successful build the builder offers to remove it and
keep just the game - it will tell you how much space that frees.

Nothing you need to play is touched: the game, your settings, your saves and any
music or graphics you added all stay. Afterwards run-build still works as a
launcher, it simply no longer offers to build. If you ever do want to rebuild,
download this package again.

You can also do it by hand. These folders inside "utils" are only for building
and are safe to delete:

      utils/tools          the build toolchain (by far the largest)
      utils/build          leftover build scratch
      utils/src            the game's source code
      utils/recomp         recompiler configuration
      utils/snesrecomp-go  runtime headers used while building
      utils/third_party    a support library used while building

Do NOT delete anything else in "utils". The game runs from inside that folder,
so "utils/config.ini", "utils/diorama-layers.ini", "utils/game-assets" and
"utils/saves" all have to stay.


IF SOMETHING GOES WRONG
-----------------------
- The browser does not open: copy the private http://127.0.0.1 URL printed in
  the run-build window and paste it into any browser on this computer.

- macOS says the file is from an unidentified developer: hold Control, click
  run-build.command, choose Open, then Open again. (You only do this once.)

@SNESBUILD_SDL_NOTE@


OPTIONAL: YOUR OWN MUSIC AND HD GRAPHICS
----------------------------------------
This package plays the ROM's original music and graphics. If you want to add
your own, look in the "utils/game-assets" folder: "manifest.ini" lists every
music and graphic slot, and you drop matching files into the "audio" and "hd"
folders beside it. Anything you don't add simply stays original.


WHAT THE FOLDERS ARE
--------------------
- run-build.*     opens the graphical builder. After the game is built this
                  opens as a launcher instead.
- run-game.*      created by the build; press it to play, every time.
- utils/          the build tools AND the files the game itself needs while
                  running - your settings, saves, and assets live here, so keep
                  it. See "free up space" above for what is safe to remove.
- utils/defaults/ this version's stock settings, kept separately so upgrading
                  never overwrites yours. Do not edit these; edit the copies in
                  utils/ instead.

Licensing and credits are in utils/LICENSE and utils/ATTRIBUTION.md.
